		{
			"id": "109859887692440844",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/109859887570287396",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:54:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> So I've had this out with many hiring managers over the years (as you might expect); the operable logic is worse than you might imagine.</p><p>Some actually think \"it's easy to hire for\" and \"we need to move fast\" will not meaningfully impact product quality in ways that will come back on them.</p><p>Others simply don't understand that a bad version of their service means that their product thesis can be totally muddied in the slow waters.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859896249064095",
			"parentId": "109859887692440844",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/109859896097063604",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:56:20.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Still others *just* got done replacing \"old timers\" who were \"expensive\" because they would push back on absolute lunacy from JS slingers. These \"not team players\" were seen as a liability, and despite the escalating expenses involved in keeping the JS folks happy, questions about costs were never actually re-examined.</p><p>So the *idea* of quality got written off in order to change the guard. How could it ever be re-asserted from within that new crew?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859898474520326",
			"parentId": "109859887692440844",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo/109859898440568638",
			"author": {
				"name": "Danny Blue",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/311/543/538/710/081/original/16eaa48f74ac1854.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:56:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>slightlyoff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I recently worked with a recruiter to look for more \"web dev\" skills even though the position was for a \"react developer\". he said more candidates are making it through the tech portion of the interviews.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859898554722528",
			"parentId": "109859896249064095",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109859898554722528",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:56:58.472Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>slightlyoff</span></a></span> Reminds me of client-side A/B testing frameworks—how merely the introduction of a large client rendering tool tanks your site performance, which ruins any result you get from both A and B</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859905236735127",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@mattpodwysocki/109859905179759482",
			"author": {
				"name": "λ Calrissian / MatthewP",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@mattpodwysocki",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/344/212/159/277/669/original/9099333c446800ef.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:58:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I was seeing so much of this, especially in the Web3 job advertisements that people were sending to me, which seemed like an interesting monoculture</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859906162885214",
			"parentId": "109859872068512493",
			"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos/109859906099830181",
			"author": {
				"name": "cthos 🐱",
				"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/028/040/622/495/original/af321586b1f6cd2d.webp"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:58:53.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> sure but that doesn’t invalidate any of the other points I made, does it?</p><p>Frameworks are abstractions we’ve built on a foundation. We can operate at the level of the framework, we did that because it’s useful. Frameworks have their own quirks and dialects, (Hell, so does WebKit vs Gecko) and if I’m running a project that speaks that dialect, who’s going to have a better time integrating if they’re junior? Senior? Principal? Pretty sure the answer changes depending on the context.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859908057171066",
			"parentId": "109859905236735127",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109859908057171066",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T22:59:23.473Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@mattpodwysocki\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>mattpodwysocki</span></a></span> when you say “this” do you mean the former or latter?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859915454352820",
			"parentId": "109859898474520326",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo/109859915408269970",
			"author": {
				"name": "Danny Blue",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@deebloo",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/311/543/538/710/081/original/16eaa48f74ac1854.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:01:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>slightlyoff</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> give me a web developer with no react experience over a react dev any day. (react === any framework)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859917214320825",
			"parentId": "109859896249064095",
			"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff/109859917105540223",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex Russell",
				"url": "https://toot.cafe/@slightlyoff",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/557/125/861/804/original/f19233215012175c.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:01:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> In the worst cases, the \"success\" of the \"big rewrite\" (note: I'm in the room, which means...yeah...it did not go that way) was seen as reason to continue down whatever path was most in vogue among the junior engineers they'd previously hired.</p><p>This becomes self-re-enforcing, as the product and engineering managers have abdicated responsibility for the product to engineering dogma.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859933511111034",
			"parentId": "109859906162885214",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109859933511111034",
