				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:15:02.496Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@mattpodwysocki\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>mattpodwysocki</span></a></span> ah, no worries!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109859981692811280",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit/109859981294304000",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stephen Belovarich",
				"url": "https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/440/938/344/080/789/original/ecec3ef32d51dd00.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:18:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p><p>A, but set expectations in the job rec about which stack the candidate needs to ramp up on. </p><p>I’ve explained to so many people JavaScript is a pre-req to React and without a solid foundation in JS the employee won’t be able to solve problems, then be ignored because the managers were convinced they knew better. They kept pushing back saying the candidates only needed to know React. There’s a fundamental lack of understanding how the web platform works at management level.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860008627782354",
			"parentId": "109859981692811280",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109860008627782354",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:24:58.058Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>iplayitofflegit</span></a></span> “There’s a fundamental lack of understanding how the web platform works at management level” oof luckily it’s been awhile since I’ve worked at a company like that!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860018178613717",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@divclassbutton/109860018141540053",
			"author": {
				"name": "xmlns=\"Dan\"",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@divclassbutton",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/388/515/213/140/840/original/0af7fdb79b555d1e.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:27:23.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I don't know React, but B is the job description I'd apply to if both of those were put in front of me.</p><p>B is low risk compared to A.</p><p>A could be anything, including a home-grown frankenstein version of React invented by Carl who has since left the company.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860020962495066",
			"parentId": "109859905236735127",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux/109860020887087181",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian LeRoux 💚",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/314/763/370/860/389/original/b7637f3827245164.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:28:05.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@mattpodwysocki\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mattpodwysocki</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> hehe a friend of mine felt web3 adopting react en masse was a bullish signal. I respectfully disagreed. 💀</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860036362952054",
			"parentId": "109860018178613717",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109860036362952054",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:32:01.258Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@divclassbutton\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>divclassbutton</span></a></span> fascinating</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860066877157620",
			"parentId": "109859981692811280",
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@divclassbutton/109860066839524781",
			"author": {
				"name": "xmlns=\"Dan\"",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@divclassbutton",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/388/515/213/140/840/original/0af7fdb79b555d1e.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:39:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>iplayitofflegit</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> that's very dependent on the job and company at hand.</p><p>I know jQuery, I know VueJS, but I've never needed to learn JS. There are a simply massive number of Devs who are working on enterprise apps that in the past would have been done (faster) in VB6, Just a bunch of buttons on some navigation bars and tables displaying data. Don't need much of anything fancy for those.</p><p>For anything client facing, sure, but even then not everyone is making figma.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860069415147730",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass/109860069392114571",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andrew Douglass",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/359/929/909/083/745/original/c4f67e7815b7a4b6.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:40:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> that’s tough. A is probably better for the recruiter to focus on, but B is important once you get there.</p><p>I had one job where specific libraries were The Way to solve specific problems as determined by a committee. Including keeping libraries pegged to version ranges across projects. It was nice to know that you wouldn’t switch between moment and date-fns depending on developer whims. BUT it was a Fortune 500 in an industry I hated.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860141558430338",
			"parentId": "109859933511111034",
			"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos/109860141474119636",
			"author": {
				"name": "cthos 🐱",
				"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/028/040/622/495/original/af321586b1f6cd2d.webp"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-13T23:58:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yes, depending on the context, seniority level, needs and demands of the role, and overall team environment.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860167041394347",
			"parentId": "109860141558430338",
			"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos/109860166978876261",
			"author": {
				"name": "cthos 🐱",
				"url": "https://mastodon.cthos.dev/@cthos",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/028/040/622/495/original/af321586b1f6cd2d.webp"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T00:05:14.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> related hypothetical: say I’m hiring a senior cloud architect. We primarily use AWS. Should I hire someone who has never architected a system on AWS before? There are enough nuances of the platform that I can’t just pick up someone who has sysadmin experience and expect them to guide other teams on AWS usage. </p><p>I think you’re talking about the inverse of “there are more people who know AWS so we should use AWS”… which is definitely one of the factors that go into a plaform decision.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860219018359181",
			"parentId": "109860008627782354",
			"url": "https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit/109860218607895688",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stephen Belovarich",
				"url": "https://uiuxdev.social/@iplayitofflegit",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/440/938/344/080/789/original/ecec3ef32d51dd00.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T00:18:22.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yeah it’s not like that at every company but been my experience where there’s a lot of Java in the stack. 😑 hoping not to contend with this in my next role.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860284428785810",
			"parentId": "109859835125195471",
			"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@eamodio/109860284390990842",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Amodio",
				"url": "https://hachyderm.io/@eamodio",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/526/684/876/341/083/original/ad2f5c45f2dca56b.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T00:35:05.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@sentience\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sentience</span></a></span> I'd go with a different C: “It’s more important that you have a solid foundation as a web developer than knowing about any specific framework, but we unfortunately use a lot of React. If you don’t already know it, you’ll have to learn it to maintain and optimize while helping us avoid it as we move forward.”</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860443080292691",
			"parentId": "109860284428785810",
