			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860560050392801",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@McNeely/109860560021646302",
			"author": {
				"name": "McNeely",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@McNeely",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/552/212/183/557/481/original/75a9716caf3885be.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T01:45:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> as a candidate I will go with A (and that's nothing to related to my opinions on React) simply due to the the fact that acknowledges that you are there to solve problems and create solutions rather than putting the focus on HOW you do  those things. Having said that I'm definitely going to ask the tech stack very early in the process.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109860753745261155",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.world/@exchgr/109860753713399351",
			"author": {
				"name": "elle mundy",
				"url": "https://mastodon.world/@exchgr",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/393/960/849/815/731/original/f7a4adecfdaf8c67.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T02:34:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> definitely A. B sounds like a horrendous mercenary dev shop that i want no part in</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109861002799798591",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@peruvianidol/109861002774140516",
			"author": {
				"name": "Mike Aparicio",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@peruvianidol",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/421/540/379/600/original/fa0833211a78cc64.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T03:37:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Both interviews will only consist of JavaScript questions. 😅</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109862095158004062",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://ruby.social/@hejsna/109862095115970068",
			"author": {
				"name": "Johan Halse",
				"url": "https://ruby.social/@hejsna",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/431/914/077/030/600/original/56fd6f8c7468349b.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T08:15:35.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> the “easy to hire” argument is so obviously broken. Unless you purposely set out to tank your velocity, you probably want to staff your team with harder-to-find people! If you do it right the search is going to take just as long whether the tech is hip or not. It’s only a good argument if your company is in ship-something-meh-and-cash-out mode.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109863489127486280",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz/109863489108067638",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jay Cruz",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/367/623/978/483/909/original/12f727267b0a863e.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T14:10:05.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I don’t buy the premise that someone that’s actually good at React, would be bad at Web Development. Like there are certainly people that are bad at React, but that’s usually because they are bad at Web Development in general. Just wanted to add this input to the convo.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109863524176204609",
			"parentId": "109863489127486280",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@walpolea/109863524107145060",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andrew Walpole",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@walpolea",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/377/935/513/666/775/original/84bf0639c7e3208a.gif"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T14:19:00.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaycruz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Anecdotally, a few years ago, I had to deal with a contract dev doing a gatsby site for us, and the react/gatsby part was decently done, but then when it came time to style it all up, they didn't know how to do CSS (everything absolutely positioned 😓, no responsiveness, etc). It was quite rough to untangle it all. That was the first time I really concretely saw that folks were learning web dev via a different path than html/css basics first.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109863535786085945",
			"parentId": "109863489127486280",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109863535786085945",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T14:21:58.228Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jaycruz</span></a></span> For sure, that makes sense to me. And in a larger sense I wouldn’t frame someone as “bad at web development“ either—“inexperienced” feels more productive</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109863715535213391",
			"parentId": "109863524176204609",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz/109863715491949299",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jay Cruz",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/367/623/978/483/909/original/12f727267b0a863e.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T15:07:40.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@walpolea\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>walpolea</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Have you heard the news? 😀 <a href=\"https://css-tricks.com/the-great-divide/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">css-tricks.com/the-great-divid</span><span class=\"invisible\">e/</span></a> For many years Web Development was mostly Backend Development and Front End was closedly tied to Web Design. But ever since “real programming” was brought to the client side, and Node happened, Web Developers that specialize on client side, don’t need to be experts in HTML and CSS any more. They don’t make websites and webpages. They can be real engineers now that build uis 🌝</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109863730033633141",
			"parentId": "109863715535213391",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@walpolea/109863729961505769",
			"author": {
				"name": "Andrew Walpole",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@walpolea",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/377/935/513/666/775/original/84bf0639c7e3208a.gif"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-14T15:11:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@jaycruz\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jaycruz</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Four years later this article is still spot-on 😩</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
